      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "No definitive moral framework justifies preemptive military strikes solely to prevent the rise of authoritarian regimes, as international law and ethical consensus generally require an imminent threat rather than speculative future actions. A just war theory approach demands strict necessity and proportionality, meaning force is only permissible if all diplomatic and non-kinetic options have absolutely failed and the threat is immediate, not a potential political shift. Therefore, nations must prioritize robust diplomatic engagement and support for international institutions over unilateral military intervention to prevent authoritarian overreach until clear red lines are crossed.",
